{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id49238297"}, "name":{"label":"Sooner Born"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2020-03-14T09:29:27-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.17"}, "id":{"label":"5660410168"}, "title":{"label":"Shady Business Practices"}, "content":{"label":"It’s bad enough this is a subscription service but the “free trial” they offer is super sketchy. If you use the free trial option, once the trial period ends you do not have an option of which billing option you can choose, they force you into the 12 month paid in advance option that’s it; which is utterly ridiculous. The shadiest most shameful part in my eyes is the fact that if you didn’t enjoy the service enough to pay the high 12 month in advance amount and decide to cancel, you don’t have up until the final second of the “trial period” like you do with literally every other subscription service I’ve ever seen, you actually have to cancel no later than 24 hours before the final second of the trial period. \n\nSo not only are you not getting the full trial period they claim, this company is Obviously doing it to try and catch people who either didn’t see the note about the 24 hours or didn’t fully understand it because it doesn’t make much sense so they can force that full 12 month advance payment even from people who have no interest whatsoever in paying upfront for 12 months. \n\nThat is extremely dishonest and bad bad business. If your product can’t speak for itself and do what it’s supposed to do while getting people excited enough about it in the process to knowingly pay the 12 month payment then the product shouldn’t be priced this high and there should be the option to go from the trial to the 30 day billing option, and maybe more effort should be put into the app design/capabilities so that more people will want you pay for it. I will never pay for this app or any others that do shady business like this. \n\nBeware everyone, watch the billing on this one...", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1154429580&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"4"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"4"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1141285695"}, "name":{"label":"midnite panther"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2020-03-10T21:24:47-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"2"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.17"}, "id":{"label":"5644234118"}, "title":{"label":"Not True AI"}, "content":{"label":"If you sign up for Mubert Pro online, then you get a glimpse into how Mubert music is made. Despite slick ultra modern graphic design, it is actually very primitive. Mubert takes prerecorded samples and arranges them randomly. It does not actually randomly generate new music (no new melodies, harmonies, or rhythms). It takes prerecorded melodies, harmonies, and rhythms and arranges them in random orders. Mubert is repetitive club muzak. I give it two stars instead of one because Mubert’s excellent  graphic design deserves a star.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1154429580&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
